inge upon the rights of other"],"id":"oewn-cease__2.42.13..","pos":"verb","src":"wn","sym":"","syn":["end","finish","stop","terminate"]},{"def":"To stop.","dna16":"8800023222000421","ex":["And with that, his twitching ceased.","After a short while, it ceased to rain."],"id":"wikt:cease:verb:4","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[],"tags":["formal","intransitive"]},{"def":"To stop doing (something).","dna16":"8800023222000520","ex":["And with that, he ceased twitching."],"id":"wikt:cease:verb:5","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[],"tags":["formal","transitive"]}]},"cease and desist":{"dna16":"8800329293000012","senses":[{"def":"To stop and not resume an action.","dna16":"8800329293000129","ex":["We are told to cease and desist or we will cease to exist."],"id":"wikt:cease and desist:verb:1","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]},{"def":"A written demand that a party stops and does not resume a certain behavior, such as copyright infringement, slander, or libel, threatening legal action if the recipient fails to do so.","dna16":"8800329293000228","ex":["She received a cease-and-desist from his solicitors soon after the podcast."],"id":"wikt:cease and desist:noun:2","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"20:1,39:1,94:1,104:1","syn":[],"tags":["attributive"]},{"def":"An order by a government agency, sanctioned by a court, that one must stop and not resume a certain (usually illegal) behavior.","dna16":"8800329293000327","ex":["His remarks did not stop the courts from issuing the cease-and-desist order."],"id":"wikt:cease and desist:noun:3","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"18:1,24:1,94:1,104:1","syn":[],"tags":["US","attributive"]}]},"cease and desist order":{"dna16":"8800023223000016","senses":[{"def":"(law) a judicial remedy issued in order to prohibit a party from doing or continuing to do a certain activity","dna16":"8800023223000123","ex":["injunctions were formerly obtained by writ but now by a judicial order"],"id":"oewn-cease_and_desist_order__1.10.